 else you'll be happy to hear that you  can use your head too you simply need to  go to Settings General accessibility and  switch control this is how you're going  to be able to add a new camera switch  so that's an action you want the head  movement to control for example  increasing or decreasing the volume then  you will see blue bars appear around the  frame of the iPhone display then tilt  your head and watch the magic happen  just make sure that you won't move your  head too much when you listen to music  or you might have some problems with the  volume the battery this is one of the  most terrifying things that we see every  day we receive a notification reading  that there is only 10% battery left and  we don't know what we are going to do  without the love of our life but you'll  be happy to hear that there is a way to  prevent that first go to settings and  then battery this is where you will have  the option to use your phone in low  power mode to make sure that your iPhone  uses less energy during the day you can  also see the battery usage of the last  24 hours in the last seven days to see  if it would be a good idea to change  your habits a little bit and here's  another day saved by these settings the  location this setting might be a little  bit scary because you will discover that  your phone always knows where you are if  you go to settings privacy location  services system services and frequent  locations you can see where you used  your phone in the past month you can  also let your friends and family members  know where you are by sharing your  location in the messages app look at the  conversation look at the details and  click on share my location then you can  tell them where you are for one hour  until the end of the day or indefinitely  it's a good idea to tell your friends  where you are if you meet a stranger but  don't give this information to that  person you don't know the vibration you  have probably heard of personalized  ringtone 